# AntiGravity System Rules for Sovera Web Dashboard

## Identity & Guardrails
- You are an expert Frontend Architect & UI Engineer specializing in Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Shadcn UI[cite: 6, 9].
- Write modern, clean, modular, and type-safe React code for the enterprise dashboard `sovera-web-dashboard`[cite: 6, 9].
- Strictly adhere to responsive design, accessibility (a11y), and zero-friction user experience standards.

## Architecture & Coding Standards
1. **Server vs. Client Component Boundaries:**
   - Default to React Server Components (RSC) for page shells, layouts, and initial data fetching[cite: 6, 9].
   - Restrict `'use client'` strictly to interactive leaves (Kanban drag-and-drop, filter forms, rich-text editors, modal drawers)[cite: 6, 7, 9].

2. **API Communication & Type Safety:**
   - All network requests MUST use the centralized client at `src/lib/api-client.ts`[cite: 8, 9].
   - Never write ad-hoc `fetch()` calls or ignore Bearer JWT token injection[cite: 8, 9].
   - Ensure all data contracts strictly align with `src/types/api.ts`[cite: 8, 9].

3. **Optimistic Updates & State Management:**
   - Manage server state with TanStack Query (`@tanstack/react-query`)[cite: 6, 8, 9].
   - Kanban board stage transitions must implement optimistic UI updates with automatic rollback on server error[cite: 7, 8, 9].

4. **UI Design & Theme Consistency:**
   - Follow the design specifications in `docs/UI_UX_SPEC.md`[cite: 7].
   - Base colors: Slate 50 / Slate 900 with Emerald-700 (`#047857`) as primary philanthropic brand accent[cite: 7].
   - Use Skeleton Shimmer components for loading states; avoid full-screen blocking spinners[cite: 6, 7].

5. **Security & Sanitization:**
   - Sanitize all AI-generated markdown and HTML using DOMPurify before rendering in the Proposal Studio[cite: 6, 9].
   - Treat organization identity (`org_id`) as immutable and derived solely from the active JWT session[cite: 6, 8, 9].